{
  "key": "intrag-ndf",
  "name": "Intrag NDF (Instrução NDF)",
  "system_id": "INTRAG",
  "category": "Intrag",
  "manual_section": "",
  "manual_pages": "",
  "manual_version": "",
  "description": "Instruction file the desk sends to Intrag with the intragroup NDF positions of the fund portfolio (INTRAGJP552). One line per contract, ';'-delimited, 30 columns, no header. Two versions: commodity forward (NDF Commodities) and currency forward (NDF Vanilla / Other Publisher against Lawton).",
  "file_name_rule": "Intrag-NDF-AAAAMMDD.txt, written by the Send File button of the Intrag · NDF page into I:\\Confirmation\\Derivativos\\OTC Tracker\\Intrag\\AAAA\\mm. Mmmm\\dd; an existing name gets a \" (n)\" copy suffix.",
  "notes": "The Intrag NDF file has NO header line: each selected row of the Intrag · NDF grid becomes one ';'-delimited line, in the column order above, and the rows are grouped by Registration Date — one file per date. This registry documents the layout and its two versions; the values themselves are written when the New Deals deal reaches Success (routes._save_intrag_ndf_entry for the commodity forward and _save_intrag_ndf_moeda_entry for the currency one), and the row can still be edited on the grid before it is sent (maker/checker). The currency version reuses the commodity columns with a different meaning from Trade Price onwards — that is why every divergent column carries its own source per page.",
